course: dictionary
lesson: 2059
title: Words of cause and effect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words show that one thing happens because of another. Consequent is a formal word for this. It means happening as a result of something. «The heavy rain and the consequent flooding» tells you the flooding came because of the rain.
explain: Look for the cause first, then the effect. The cause is what starts things off, like the rain. The effect is what follows, like the flooding. Consequently is the adverb, and it means «as a result» or «so».
explain: The sentence «Running an "if" backwards is a mistake grown-ups call affirming the consequent» uses the word for the part that comes after as a result. You do not need to know the whole rule yet. Notice that the word names what follows, and that is its job.
fact: Consequent means happening as a result of something.
fact: «Consequently» means «as a result» or «so».
fact: Consequent is often used with on or upon, as in consequent on or consequent upon.
fact: Formal words like consequent are used in reports, science write-ups and exam answers.
fact: A quick check is to swap in «as a result» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The heavy rain and the consequent flooding closed the road.» What does consequent mean here? | Happening before the rain | Quiet and calm | *Happening as a result of the rain | Very heavy and wet
exercise: Find the word that means «as a result». | ancient | quietly | barely | *consequently
exercise: Ella says consequent is just another word for funny. Is she right? | No, it means quiet | *No, it means happening as a result of something | Yes, it means funny | Yes, it means very old
test: In «The team trained every day, and consequent improvements were clear», what was the cause? | Clear weather | *Training every day | Eating lunch early | Winning the cup
test: It rained all day, ___ the match was cancelled. Which word fills the gap? | ancient | *consequently | barely | quietly
exam: Which statement about consequent is true? | It means only just | *It means happening as a result of something | It means giving out light | It means very old
